        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The composite function adds $4$ to the input, giving the answers in a–d.",
          "worked": "Using $f(f(x))=x+4$:\n$$\\begin{align*}f(f(0))&=0+4=4\\\\f(f(3))&=3+4=7\\\\f(f(-1))&=-1+4=3\\\\f(f(-8))&=-8+4=-4\\end{align*}$$\nEach answer is $4$ more than the original input, agreeing with a–d.",
